From: anonymous <anonymous@bazzite.taild619.ts.net>
Date: Thu, 9 Jul 2026 13:04:44 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 5/6] fix(tts): derive voice quality tier from Apple-style ids
 in /voices/all

Servers that wrap macOS system voices (e.g. macos-speech-server) return
/v1/audio/voices/all entries with quality omitted or hardcoded to
'default', even though the tier is encoded in the Apple voice id
(com.apple.voice.<tier>.<lang>.<Name>). The rich path accepted entries
verbatim, so the premium/enhanced badges and quality-first ordering
never activated against such servers.

Extract the rich-path parsing into parseOpenAITTSVoicesAll, which keeps
a meaningful server-provided quality but otherwise derives the tier via
the existing inferVoiceFromId helper. Malformed entries are dropped so
fetchVoices still falls back to the flat voice list.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Fable 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
